[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4912896469","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121081#issuecomment-4912896469","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121081","id":4912896469,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABJNTZ1Q","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-08T08:32:37Z","updated_at":"2026-07-08T08:32:48Z","body":"I appreciate the tests, and it does look like it's a bit faster than before.\r\n\r\nHowever, the code needs to be seen in context. `Dictionary` is a type only used for scripting and communications (high performance applications use `AHashMap`). The overhead of communications is likely to outweigh the overhead of `Dictionary` itself by several orders of magnitude (not to speak of cold calls where several dereferences are required to get to the data). \r\n\r\nPractically, a difference of 20ns per call is unlikely to be felt in any real scenario i can think of, and thus i'm not sure if it's worth the new code / extra case added here.\r\n","author_association":"MEMB